20:["$","p","The five-stage model was originally observed in dying patients, not the bereaved, and was never intended as a checklist. Grief does not progress tidily, and revisiting an earlier feeling is not regression.",{"className":"text-base leading-relaxed text-body","children":"The five-stage model was originally observed in dying patients, not the bereaved, and was never intended as a checklist. Grief does not progress tidily, and revisiting an earlier feeling is not regression."}]
21:["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-line bg-surface p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-serif text-xl text-ink","children":"Symptom mechanics"}],[["$","p","Current models describe grief as moving back and forth between confronting the loss and attending to ongoing life. Both are necessary. A morning of laughter does not undo mourning, and a wave of sorrow two years on is not a relapse.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"Current models describe grief as moving back and forth between confronting the loss and attending to ongoing life. Both are necessary. A morning of laughter does not undo mourning, and a wave of sorrow two years on is not a relapse."}],["$","p","Grief also lives in the body: appetite changes, disrupted sleep, chest heaviness, and a real hit to concentration and immune function. This is why practical care — food, water, sleep — is legitimate grief work.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"Grief also lives in the body: appetite changes, disrupted sleep, chest heaviness, and a real hit to concentration and immune function. This is why practical care — food, water, sleep — is legitimate grief work."}]]]}]
